    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="0736" n="478" xml:id="pg478"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1992C</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-19T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 19, 1915, 3 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1969. Department’s 1965, July 18, 7 p. m. In any discussion arising over
                    Bernstorff’s message you should make it clear that the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lusitania</hi> case is incidental to issue of principle as to safeguarding
                    neutrals on the high seas; that admission of liability as to Americans on <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lusitania</hi> will not be sufficient unless avoidance
                    of future acts is substantially assured.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
